  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed change of use to a House in Multiple Occupation (Use Class C4), together with existing conversions, would result in more than one converted property within a consecutive row of five dwellings, exceeding Policy DMD 5 thresholds. This overconcentration would materially harm the established character and function of this predominantly single-family residential section of Brettenham Road, contrary to Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD 5 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).",
    "The proposed refuse and recycling storage, by reason of its siting immediately adjacent to the window serving ground floor front Bedroom (labelled as Bedroom 1), would result in potential noise, disturbance and odour impacts, thereby providing an unsatisfactory standard of accommodation and harming the living conditions of future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Chapters 12 and 14 of the NPPF (2026), Policies D3 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD5, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
